Provenance & retained upstream notice
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

self.language-eval is a fully vendored, renamed fork of EleutherAI's Language
Model Evaluation Harness (https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness),
originally licensed MIT. It was previously carried as self.lm-evaluation-harness;
the Python package was renamed lm_eval -> language_eval.

Why fully vendored: self.ai licenses the combined work under GPLv3. MIT is
one-way compatible with GPLv3, so the upstream code is included here under GPLv3
while its original MIT license text and attribution are retained in
LICENSE.eleutherai-mit. A GPLv3 combined work cannot be contributed back to an
MIT upstream, so self.language-eval is a hard vendor: we do not track or push to
the original project. self.language-eval is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
connected to EleutherAI.

self.language-eval is the catch-all harness for language-focused evaluation
tasks; more specific language-eval harnesses are forked from it.

The original MIT license text is preserved verbatim in LICENSE.eleutherai-mit.
